PERSPECTIVE LADDER READOUT
  R(1)=1 == A(2)=1
  R(2)=2 == A(3)=2
  R(3)=4 == A(4)=4
  R(4)=12 == A(5)=12
  R(5)=48 != A(6)=56
  R(6)=296 != A(7)=456
The equality R(n)=A(n+1) holds through n=4 and fails at n=5.

DUPLICATION LAW
The line sheet has k(k+1) apparent binary values but only 2k degrees of freedom.
The one-point extension layer has 2^n apparent incident words per labelled parent,
but only Burnside word-orbits per parent class.  Both are the same doctrine:
keep the boundary/address carrier, then quotient by the stabilizer at the last step.

TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS
  vertices=layer carriers: boundary words, rank-one sheets, parent classes, rooted children, unrooted children
  observable=amount of route/perspective information retained before quotient
  switch/gauge=more retained information points to less retained information
  tie Hamiltonian path=boundary_words > rank_one_sheet > parent_word_orbit > rooted_child > unrooted_child
  challenged assumption=vertices are not original tournament vertices; they are extension carriers/proof states
  preserves=one-vertex extension and fixed-path layer address
  destroys=which child root/deletion address produced an unrooted class
